  "body": "Found while fixing #1190.\n\n**What happens.** The door that keeps a milling operation off a lathe's work spindle (`app::lathe_voice::at_post`, #1190) fires when the post script declares the turning dialect in its manifest: `capabilities` with the turning bit (2). Every shipped post states the mask (2 for `fanuc-lathe.cps` and `tormach-lathe.cps`, 1 for the rest), and a copy of a shipped lathe post carries the line with it. A user's own turning script that declares no `capabilities` at all is read as \"not turning\", so the door does not fire for it: a milling pass that stays on one meridian would post through it as before #1190 (work spindle at the cutter's rpm), with only the script's own meridian check in the way.\n\n**Expected.** A script whose dialect is not stated is not silently treated as a mill post where that matters. Options to decide between: (a) the engine refuses by name a script with no `capabilities` declaration (\"this post script does not say whether it is a milling or a turning post - add `capabilities = 1` or `capabilities = 2`\"), which changes behaviour for existing user scripts and for the many small inline test scripts; (b) on a lathe or mill-turn machine only, an undeclared script is held to the lathe door; (c) the post authoring notes state the manifest line as required and the app warns once when it is missing.\n\n**Evidence.** `crates/post/src/post/dialect.rs` (`speaks_turning`: no mask reads as not turning), `crates/app/src/lathe_voice.rs` (`at_post`), decision `docs/decisions/1190-mill-op-on-lathe-post.md` (\"Left open\").\n\nDone means: one of the options is chosen and recorded; a turning script without the manifest line can no longer post a milling section on the work spindle unnoticed, pinned by a test with an inline undeclared lathe script.\n",
